  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 0.3.8, package.json says 1.0.0.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "php-extensions",
      "lines": [
        "1 PHP extension is required by composer but not listed as <lib> in appinfo/info.xml:",
        "  iconv (opis/string)",
        "  A Nextcloud server need not load it. The server checks <lib> before it enables the app; composer only checks where it runs. Without the <lib> the app is enabled anyway and the first call into the extension fails at runtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "node-eol",
      "lines": [
        "engines.node ^20.0.0 in package.json admits only end-of-life Node lines: the release is built on Node 20, which reached end of life on 2026-04-30.",
        "  That Node receives no security fixes, and the lockfile is resolved for it. The oldest line still maintained is Node 22.",
        "  Node release dates from schedule.json in nodejs/Release, as of 2026-10-23."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "script-without-config",
      "lines": [
        "composer.json scripts test, coverage run phpunit with phpunit.xml, which is not in the checkout.",
        "  cd tests/php/ && phpunit -c phpunit.xml",
        "  The command is there to be run, so whoever runs it gets a tool that has nothing to go by - and CI, if it runs the script, reports the failure as the change under test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "schema/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Validator.php:37 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks it and the app fails in the code that reads it, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += schema ships it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml, package.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No SPDX id: agpl (package.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is certificate24, the checkout directory is nextcloud-certificate24.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 28 to 32; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 28 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^20.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
